# netsurf: inline style object reads the attribute, ignores garbage writes (patch 361)
# Generated 2026-11-01
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 360)
#
# el.style (the el-helpers style object in macsurf_qjs.c) had two faults,
# both against what Chromium does:
#
#  - It read only what a script had set. Values authored in the style
#    attribute read '' -- style="display:none" answered '' to
#    el.style.display, so the usual toggle
#    `el.style.display = el.style.display === 'none' ? '' : 'none'`
#    hid an already hidden menu again. Reads now parse the LIVE
#    attribute (quote- and paren-aware, the last declaration wins,
#    custom properties keep their case), which also feeds
#    getComputedStyle's inline fallback.
#  - A write removed the old declaration and stored any value. JS
#    arithmetic garbage -- `w + "px"` with w undefined -- is what fixes1087
#    deliberately produces for a size measured before layout, expecting a
#    no-op; here it deleted an authored width:200px and stored
#    width:undefinedpx, which libcss drops, so the block went full width.
#    A value holding NaN, undefined, null, Infinity or [object X], bare or
#    with a unit, is now ignored and the old value kept. Exempt: --custom
#    properties and those taking custom idents or strings (font-family,
#    font, content, quotes, grid-area/row/column/template-areas,
#    animation*, transition*, counter-*, list-style*, will-change,
#    view-transition-name). null and '' still remove, as in browsers. The
#    cssText setter drops only such declarations.
#
# Also: setProperty honours "important" and getPropertyPriority exists;
# removeProperty returns the old value. The attribute keeps its
# serialization (name:value;name:value). Not covered: shorthands do not
# expand (style.marginTop of an authored `margin: 5px` reads ''), and
# values Chromium rejects for other reasons (an unknown keyword) are still
# stored -- libcss drops them at render as before.
#
# Gate: JS-style-invalid (file:// snapshot: authored width:200px survives
# an undefined/NaN write-back; an authored display:none is toggled
# shown); full gate361 exit 0. Scorecard, all 21 sites against the
# r79-360 reference, this patch and the patch-360 binary back to back
# (r86-361 / r86-pre361): mean 74.54 vs 74.56 -- no regression. The
# movers are live content: stackoverflow 64.8 vs 65.6 reran interleaved
# at 65.4 / 64.1 (361) vs 65.3 / 18.5 (360, a challenge page), text
# recall 0.50-0.53 either way.
#
